连分式的组合理论方面的专家。\n\n七、主办单位\n\n数学与交叉科学研究中心\n\n〖供稿单位：数学与交叉科学研究中心     作者：杨媛    责任编辑：卞悦悦 蒋晓涵〗--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConnectivity of old and new models of friends-and-strangers graphs (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0196885823001860)\nciteturn0search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 months ago; In this paper, we investigate the connectivity of friends-and-strangers graphs, which were introduced by Defant and Kravitz in 2020.\n\n## Advances in Applied Mathematics\n\nVolume 155, April 2024, 102668\n\n# Connectivity of old and new models of friends-and-strangers graphs\n\nhttps://doi.org/10.1016/j.aam.2023.102668Get rights and content\n\n## Abstract\n\nIn this paper, we investigate the connectivity of friends-and-strangers graphs, which were introduced by Defant and Kravitz in 2020. We begin by considering friends-and-strangers graphs arising from two random graphs and consider the threshold probability at which such graphs attain maximal connectivity. We slightly improve the lower bounds on the threshold probabilities, thus disproving two conjectures of Alon, Defant and Kravitz. We also improve the upper bound on the threshold probability in the case of random bipartite graphs, and obtain a tight bound up to a factor of {n}^{o(1)}${n}^{o(1)}$. Further, we introduce a generalization of the notion of friends-and-strangers graphs in which vertices of the starting graphs are allowed to have multiplicities and obtain generalizations of previous results of Wilson and of Defant and Kravitz in this new setting.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEquidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/350371837_Equidistributions_around_special_kinds_of_descents_and_excedances)\nciteturn0search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 months ago; In a recent paper ({arXiv:2101.01928v1}) Baril and Kirgizov posed two conjectures on the equidistibution of $(cyc, des_2)\\sim (cyc, pex)$ and $(des, des_2)\\sim (exc, pex)$, where cyc, des and exc are classical statistics counting the numbers of cycles, descents and excedances of permutation, while $des_2$ and pex are numbers of special descents and excedances over permutations. In this paper, using combinatorial theory of J-continued fractions and bijections we confirm and strengthen the second conjecture and expand the first one.\n\n# Equidistributions around special kinds of descents and excedances\n\n  * March 2021\n\nDOI:10.48550/arXiv.2103.13092\n\nAuthors:\n\nBin Han\n\n  * University of Gothenburg\n\nJianxi Mao\n\n  * Dalian University of Technology\n\nJiang Zeng\n\n  * Claude Bernard University Lyon 1\n\n## Abstract\n\nIn a recent paper ({arXiv:2101.01928v1}) Baril and Kirgizov posed two conjectures on the equidistibution of $(cyc, des_2)\\sim (cyc, pex)$ and $(des, des_2)\\sim (exc, pex)$, where cyc, des and exc are classical statistics counting the numbers of cycles, descents and excedances of permutation, while $des_2$ and pex are numbers of special descents and excedances over permutations. In this paper, using combinatorial theory of J-continued fractions and bijections we confirm and strengthen the second conjecture and expand the first one.\n\n\n## No file available\n\nImage: Request Full-text Paper PDF\n\nTo read the file of this research,\nyou can request a copy directly from the authors.\n\nRequest file PDF\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nConnectivity of old and new models of friends-and-strangers graphs (https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0196885823001860)\nciteturn0search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.6 years ago; Crawled: 3 months ago; In this paper, we disprove this conjecture by showing that , using a slightly tweaked version of the original argument from [1]. ... If the total multiplicity of Y is n, we define a multiplicity friends-and-stranger